docs {
  # GET /api/artworks/artworks/:slug/status/ — Live artwork sale status

  Returns the live sale `status` and prices of a single artwork. Read-only
  on the hot path; a stale `reserved` hold (expired session from a closed
  tab or abandoned Checkout) is reconciled against Stripe and persisted
  before responding — Stripe-expired returns `available`, Stripe-paid
  returns `sold`, still-open/unreachable keeps `reserved`.
  Feeds the landing BuyWidget island: baked static HTML
  paints fast, then this call swaps the buy form for a Vendida/Reservada
  badge when the live status differs.
  Public endpoint, no `Authorization` header. Throttled: `artwork_status`
  120/hour per client (`429` when exceeded — wait and retry).

  Takes no request body and no query params.

  Replace `ciudad-reflejada` below with any active artwork slug (seed slugs
  work; unknown slugs, inactive artworks, or inactive artists return `404`).
  Call once per artwork detail-page mount, fire-and-forget: never block
  render, never retry on failure — on any error keep the baked HTML.

  ## Status codes

  - `200 OK` — live status, returns slug, status, prices, and timestamp
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown slug, inactive artwork, or inactive artist
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — throttled (120 status checks/hour per client)

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "slug": "ciudad-reflejada",
    "status": "sold",
    "status_display": "Vendida",
    "price_mxn": "12500.00",
    "price_usd": "750.00",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-18T14:22:00Z"
  }
  ```

  `status` is `available`, `sold`, `reserved`, `on_loan`, or
  `not_available`. `status_display` is the Spanish label. Prices are
  decimal strings. Response carries `Cache-Control: no-store`.

  ## Error (404/429)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Not found.",
    "data": {}
  }
  ```
}
